„­bible_version£KJV¤book=§chapter¨sectionsœ…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjand he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for our's only, but also for the sins of the whole world.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdHe that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjBut whoso keepeth his word, in him verily is the love of God perfected: hereby know we that we are in him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQHe that saith he abideth in him ought himself also so to walk, even as he walked.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®Brethren, I write no new commandment unto you, but an old commandment which ye had from the beginning. The old commandment is the word which ye have heard from the beginning.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAgain, a new commandment I write unto you, which thing is true in him and in you: because the darkness is past, and the true light now shineth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXHe that saith he is in the light, and hateth his brother, is in darkness even until now.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`He that loveth his brother abideth in the light, and there is none occasion of stumbling in him.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–But he that hateth his brother is in darkness, and walketh in darkness, and knoweth not whither he goeth, because that darkness hath blinded his eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZI write unto you, little children, because your sins are forgiven you for his name's sake.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛI write unto you, fathers, because ye have known him that is from the beginning. I write unto you, young men, because ye have overcome the wicked one. I write unto you, little children, because ye have known the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛI have written unto you, fathers, because ye have known him that is from the beginning. I have written unto you, young men, because ye are strong, and the word of God abideth in you, and ye have overcome the wicked one.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Love not the world, neither the things that are in the world. If any man love the world, the love of the Father is not in him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor all that is in the world, the lust of the flesh, and the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life, is not of the Father, but is of the world.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeAnd the world passeth away, and the lust thereof: but he that doeth the will of God abideth for ever.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥Little children, it is the last time: and as ye have heard that antichrist shall come, even now are there many antichrists; whereby we know that it is the last time.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉThey went out from us, but they were not of us; for if they had been of us, they would no doubt have continued with us: but they went out, that they might be made manifest that they were not all of us.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙABut ye have an unction from the Holy One, and ye know all things.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsI have not written unto you because ye know not the truth, but because ye know it, and that no lie is of the truth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrWho is a liar but he that denieth that Jesus is the Christ? He is antichrist, that denieth the Father and the Son.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrWhosoever denieth the Son, the same hath not the Father: (but) he that acknowledgeth the Son hath the Father also.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂLet that therefore abide in you, which ye have heard from the beginning. If that which ye have heard from the beginning shall remain in you, ye also shall continue in the Son, and in the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd this is the promise that he hath promised us, even eternal life.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEThese things have I written unto you concerning them that seduce you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñBut the anointing which ye have received of him abideth in you, and ye need not that any man teach you: but as the same anointing teacheth you of all things, and is truth, and is no lie, and even as it hath taught you, ye shall abide in him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book=§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆAnd now, little children, abide in him; that, when he shall appear, we may have confidence, and not be ashamed before him at his coming.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`If ye know that he is righteous, ye know that every one that doeth righteousness is born of him.¦layout ªlast_verse